        "![](images/newplot.png)\n",
        "\n",
        "All in all, I think the results were...okay?\n",
        "\n",
        "NLP certainly has limitations and I could have probably refined some of the steps along the way. For instance, I could have removed some of the SEC specific stopwords. When it comes to topic modelling, I realized it wasn't much of a value add because the raw text has already been categorized in different topics such as 'Supply and Concentration of Chips, Memory, and Data Center Equipment' and 'Electrical Power and Fuel Constraints'. Now if this was an unsupervised learning task, wherein I had to find topics, then I think topic modelling would had been pretty useful. Finally, you might be wondering \"why didn't I simply run this analysis via a LLM?\"\n",
        "\n",
        "My answer is:\n",
        "\n",
        "```{=html}\n",
        "<p><div class=\"tenor-gif-embed\" data-postid=\"10681570624129307805\" data-share-method=\"host\" data-aspect-ratio=\"1.76596\" data-width=\"100%\"><a href=\"https://tenor.com/view/tony-stark-limited-tech-meme-technology-gif-10681570624129307805\">Tony Stark Limited GIF</a>from <a href=\"https://tenor.com/search/tony+stark-gifs\">Tony Stark GIFs</a></div> <script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://tenor.com/embed.js\"></script></p>\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "```{=html}\n",
        "<p><div class=\"tenor-gif-embed\" data-postid=\"4796147180375266924\" data-share-method=\"host\" data-aspect-ratio=\"1.09756\" data-width=\"100%\"><a href=\"https://tenor.com/view/westworld-of-course-not-nature-of-your-reality-doloresabernathy-gif-4796147180375266924\">Westworld Of-course-not GIF</a>from <a href=\"https://tenor.com/search/westworld-gifs\">Westworld GIFs</a></div> <script type=\"text/javascript\" async src=\"https://tenor.com/embed.js\"></script></p>\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Don't get me wrong. I did think long and hard about using a LLM to extract insights. But then I thought to myself \"how would it be any different than simply uploading the filing and asking a LLM to summarize the key insights?\" Also I do have gemma4:12b running locally on my PC. At the time, I just didn't see the utility in using a LLM to summarize key insights of a S-1 filing by a company that also provides one of the most popular LLMs. That being said, I do see an opportunity to use LLMs for enhancing topic modelling. Turns out BERTopic has a [functionality](https://maartengr.github.io/BERTopic/getting_started/representation/llm.html#llama-manual-quantization)to generate better labels for the topics.\n",
        "\n",
        "So there it is, an extremely bare bones NLP analysis of Anthropic's Risk Factors listed in its S-1 filing. Maybe this analysis didn't result in the giving me detailed insights that I was expecting. But at the very least, I learned a thing or two but some new avenues I can explore for future projects!"
